#VRML V2.0 utf8
# Ion Garden Speaker -- an original six-channel radial speaker array for the
# Cybertown Revival Mall.  Generated by build-ion-garden-speaker.py;
# edit that, not this.
#
# Touch the speaker -- any part of the amplifier head -- to power the system on:
# the six speaker leaves open
# outward into a listening bloom and the core, the dome and the leaf accents
# light.  Touch it again to power off -- the glow stops on its next beat and the
# leaves fold back.  The dome stands above the closed leaves, so it is reachable
# in either state.
#
# This is a speaker that stays silent: audio nodes are forbidden in Mall
# objects, and the emitter gates their absence.
#
# The wording above is deliberate, and the words this header avoids are avoided
# on purpose.  WRLForge's validator -- and, more to the point, anything else
# that screens an upload -- looks for the forbidden node names as PLAIN
# SUBSTRINGS, so naming one in a comment fails the file on the strength of a
# sentence explaining that the node is not there.  Measured: an earlier draft of
# this header named the audio node once, and `validate()` returned ok = false on
# an object that has never contained one.  The build's own gate judges node
# SYNTAX on the comment-stripped text and is unaffected either way, but the
# shipped file has to survive the naive scan too -- so it simply never says the
# names.  See notes.md, which is free to spell them out.

WorldInfo {
  title "Ion Garden Speaker"
  info [
    "Made By: BassMekanik"
    "Uploaded: September, 2026"
    "Category: Electronics"
    "Limited To: 35"
    "Mall Price: 65 CC"
    "Touch the speaker to open its six channels. Touch it again to close."
  ]
}


